h(55, 350, """What has never been said before! The chain of the wording (allegiance is given to him under compulsion, unwillingly) is not sound! But why is "under compulsion, unwillingly" plausible? What no one has explained before!""")

t(55, 1105, """Who do these people worship?! Is it the very same God we worship?! Allah? Or another god we do not know? Do these people worship the very Allah we worship, while they bow, prostrate, fast and glorify, then harm people? Then steal from people? Then devour inheritances? Then oppress and do every evil? Then commit every abomination?! Is He the same God we worship, pray to and fast for, is it Him they worship?! No. It is impossible that they worship the same God we worship. Impossible. What is clear is that we worship a God other than the one they worship, because we worship a God who does not tell us, "After prostrating to Me, commit every abomination and evil on earth." As for these, they finish their prostration, say the salam, and do what our God has forbidden. So while prostrating, were they worshipping Allah who forbids doing evil, or were they worshipping a lord other than Allah?!""")

h(55, 1900, """Who exactly do we worship? Our Mighty Lord says on the tongue of His Khalil: "Then what is your thought about the Lord of the worlds?" (87)""")

t(56, 125, """I read comments by some brothers and sisters whose overall meaning revolves around one issue: we are anxious about our loved ones!

To these brothers and sisters I say: You are heading toward hard days that all people will face, and in them people will be two kinds, no third: a kind like you who will die of anxiety, and a kind who relied on his Lord and entrusted his loved ones to Allah the Mighty, with whom trusts are never lost.

As for those who decided to be anxious, very severe days will pass over them.. As for those who decided to entrust their loved ones to the One with whom trusts are never lost, they have made Allah their guardian, and that is good and salvation for their loved ones, if Allah the Exalted wills. And those who decided to be anxious did not make Allah their guardian, and there is no good in this for their loved ones.

So entrust them to Allah, for man is too weak to save even a small ant.""")

h(56, 1250, """Who has not prepared?!""")

t(56, 1910, """A Muslim young man contacted me a while ago, weeping.. At the start of his words I thought he was ill, or had lost money, or missed a chance to emigrate, or a girl he loved had rejected him. But on listening to the end, his weeping was for none of this. He was weeping because he had tasted the sweetness of the night prayer, then was no longer able to pray at night.

The story of this young man is a recurring example for many, and I relate it to remind of two matters:
First: this is truly something worth weeping over, and something the heart truly aches for. As for those weeping over a worldly thing they did not get, wretched weepers are they.
The second matter: Beware of despair. I wept this weeping for 5 years and did not despair for a single day, and I knew, trusting in Allah, that I would return to this great obedience. So beware of weeping the weeping of the despairing; weep the weeping of the longing, for it is the best weeping you can weep. The world took me, turning me over and scattering me, from 2016 to 2022, from its far east to its middle, then to its western borders, like the shaking of water in a waterskin. Then in a dream in late 2016, two noble angels on my right and left who prayed the night with me each folded his prayer mat, and my prayer mat was folded; I knew it was the last night. And indeed after that I was driven out of my home, humiliated and expelled, and I roamed the earth to its far east, then its middle, then its western borders, and the world kept chasing me with its exhausting problems until early 2022. So did I think I had been cast away, and weep the weeping of the despairing?!""")

t(57, 60, """No, by Allah, I did not weep the weeping of the despairing even once; but I wept the weeping of the longing for five years, until the moment came when the door opened again. It was not a casting away, because commitment, by the grace of Allah the Exalted, was stronger than in 2016. So watch yourself, watch your religion; watch the level of taqwa in your heart, the level of your love of good in your heart, the level of your gentleness with people, the level of your endurance of people's injustice, and the level of your ability to forgive the wrongdoer. Then you will know you have not been cast away. No one knows the reason for the pause but Allah the Exalted, so do not despair. As long as you weep the weeping of the longing, and as long as you advance in commitment upward, not downward, know that you will return to the sweetness of the night prayer, if Allah the Exalted wills. Know it with the knowledge of one certain and confident of his Mighty Lord's love for him, and do not despair.""")

h(57, 900, """Beware of despair. A young man weeps in pain, not over money, nor the world, nor emigration to the West!""")

