t(59, 1760, """Some brothers thought from the post about this weak narration that I was calling the narration a lie and believed it was fabricated in the name of the Companion on whom it stops. It is not a matter of calling it fabricated, but only a warning about the weakness of the narration's chain, for the sake of scholarly honesty.
This was the text of the post:
-------------------------
This hadith is weak in its chain and is not established from the Prophet ﷺ.

The hadith is narrated with the following wording: "The people will perform Hajj together and stand at Arafah together without an imam..." "Yu'arrifun" means they attend Arafah. It is a hadith about the events of the end of time, the signs of the Hour and the appearance of the Mahdi, and it is mawquf, not marfu'!

The grade of the hadith and the views of the scholars of jarh wa ta'dil
Ruling of the hadith scholars: The hadith is very weak; the hadith scholars judged it weak and munkar.

Defect of the chain: Al-Hakim narrated it in "al-Mustadrak" and Nu'aym ibn Hammad in "al-Fitan", and in its chain is a narrator called Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydullah al-Fazari (Abu 'Awn), who is abandoned in hadith and very weak according to the scholars of jarh wa ta'dil.""")

t(60, 60, """Nature of the text: The hadith is classed by scholars among the "mawqufat" (that is, from the words of the Companion 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, may Allah be pleased with them both, and not raised to the Prophet ﷺ); even so, the chain itself is ruined, and its attribution even to the Companion is not sound!

The full text of the hadith, for information
The hadith is narrated with the weak chain as follows: "The people will perform Hajj together and stand at Arafah together without an imam. While they are camped at Mina, something like rabies (that is, turmoil and fighting) seizes them, and the tribes rise against one another and fight until al-'Aqabah flows with blood. So they flee to the best of them, and come to him while he is weeping with his face pressed to the Ka'bah... and allegiance is given to him unwillingly... for he is the Mahdi on earth.\"""")

h(60, 1000, """Notice""")

t(60, 1705, """Renaissance has a key: states rise through much work and collapse through much talk. Whoever is tried with any part of this matter in the future, let his speech be action, his action earnestness, and his earnestness commitment. As for one who grasps the state of people today and the reality of most of them, he is closer to fleeing from them, the flight of one escaping an oven kindled by their fitnas and their greed, whose fire never dies down.. But perhaps Allah, our Mighty Lord, holy are His names and attributes, great in the heavens and on earth, exalted be He greatly, will raise up for our Ummah from its youth branches that had bent, and set right the state of the minds of its sons and daughters, ruins that had settled, stilled and taken root in their homes. Through the stars of the people of guidance Allah guides His servants to the right path that was veiled from them; with sincere forearms rolled up, the heap of a hundred years is lifted; by longing for Allah the Mighty, hearts are set right and intentions gleam like pure diamond. Then words succeed in influence and enlightenment, deeds bear fruit in success after success, and the Ummah rises by the permission of its Lord.""")

h(61, 150, """If the Ummah's action prevails over its talk, it has risen""")

