t(67, 1005, """Why is Europe collapsing economically while people do not know?! (The common people of the world's societies, and even the common people of the Europeans themselves) do not know!

The last point in the article is the most dangerous!!

Europe currently (in 2026) suffers from a real ((structural defect)) in its economy that threatens its global competitiveness. This defect is not due to a temporary crisis; rather it is the result of an accumulation of deep structural problems, which official reports such as the "Draghi Report" described as a "slow agony" resulting from prolonged neglect!!

After the cut-off of Russian gas, European industries (especially in Germany) suffer from a permanent rise in energy costs compared with their competitors in the United States and China.

This led to a wave of record bankruptcies in Western European companies and a decline in the competitiveness of heavy products, and this is happening for the first time since the era of modern European renaissance in the world order of 1945.

Europe also faces a growing shortage of skilled labour due to the retirement of the baby-boom generation and declining birth rates.

This shift imposes enormous pressures on pension funds and health-care systems, which drains public budgets.

The continent has failed to secure a leading position in advanced technology fields such as artificial intelligence, cloud computing and digitisation compared with America and China.

Many emerging tech companies prefer to flee to American markets because of the complexity of regulatory laws in Europe and the lack of bold financing.

Growth of the eurozone economy is expected to hover around only 1.1% to 1.2% in 2026.

Declining productivity: Individual productivity has suffered stagnation for years, which hinders raising real living standards and creates an unreal bubble economy. The false services economy, which is not an economy at all.

The strict regulatory bureaucracy of the European Union curbs companies' flexibility and hinders the speed of their growth in the global market.""")

t(68, 60, """The most dangerous point, which the reports do not mention or talk about, and which I find more dangerous than everything above: the decline of Europe's military capacity to forcibly secure the flow of oil and gas to it, which will make it in the future literally a ((hostage)) in the hands of the rising Middle East as a striking world power.""")

